# ─── Security Token ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only secret guarding the HTTP POST /api/stats/* endpoints (admin/tool
# access). Game clients never use it — they submit stats over the socket.
# Deliberately NOT prefixed with VITE_ so Vite can never compile it into the
# public client bundle. Set a strong random value in production
# (e.g. openssl rand -hex 32).
API_TOKEN=tutto-local-dev-token

# ─── Backend (Node / Express) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port the Express server listens on (default: 3001).
PORT=3001

# Allowed CORS origin for both the HTTP API and the Socket.IO server.
#   unset, NODE_ENV != production : '*' (any origin) — fine for local dev/LAN play.
#   unset, NODE_ENV == production : same-origin only. The frontend is served by
#                                   this same server, so this is the right
#                                   default for a normal deployment.
#   set                           : exactly that origin, in any environment.
# Setting it explicitly to '*' in production is refused at startup — that would
# let any site make authenticated cross-origin requests. Set the real origin
# instead when the frontend is served from somewhere else, e.g.:
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://tutto.example.com
#
# Deliberately left UNSET rather than assigned. This file is copied to .env as
# the first setup step, so a value here follows the deployer into production —
# and this one used to be '*', which the startup guard refuses, so
# `npm run start:prod` exited 1 for anyone who had followed the README. Unset
# already means '*' in development, so the line bought local play nothing.

# Whether exactly one reverse proxy fronts this server. Set to 1 ONLY then:
# per-IP rate limiting will read real client addresses from X-Forwarded-For
# instead of seeing every user as the proxy. Deliberately left UNSET here —
# this file is copied to .env, and on a directly exposed server (including
# LAN play) trusting that header would let any client forge its own
# rate-limit identity. A production start without it logs a one-line
# reminder in case the proxy case applies.
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# Per-IP cap on new Socket.IO connections: at most 30 per 10-second window.
# The window is fixed; this overrides only the 30, for the rare deployment
# where one address legitimately stands for many players (a large NAT'd
# venue). Counted per client address — which behind a reverse proxy is only
# the real client with TRUST_PROXY=1 above. Junk or non-positive values are
# ignored. The test suites set it huge for their bursts of local connections
# (vite.config.ts, playwright.config.ts); a normal deployment leaves it unset.
# SOCKET_CONN_LIMIT_MAX=100

# Keeps one live line at the bottom of the server's console saying whether a
# game is in progress — i.e. whether restarting would interrupt anyone. Rooms
# live only in the running process, so this is the last chance to ask. The line
# is rewritten in place on a terminal and never scrolls; see README, "Restart
# safety".
# Deliberately left UNSET here. This file is copied to .env, which every
# non-Docker start loads — including the servers the test suites spawn and read
# stdout from, and every `npm run dev` session. start-tutto-prod.bat sets it for
# the one window that wants it. Uncomment only to get the line everywhere.
# TUTTO_STATUS_LINE=1

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute path to the SQLite database file. Exists for deployments that must
# keep the database outside the application directory — the Docker image sets
# DB_PATH=/data/stats.db so the database lives on a mounted volume instead of
# inside the image. It wins over everything below.
# DB_PATH=/data/stats.db
#
# Left unset, the file depends on NODE_ENV:
#   production (the Docker image, `npm run start:prod`) → server/stats.db
#   anything else (`npm run server`, `npm start`)       → server/stats.dev.db
# So a development server on a machine that also runs the real thing keeps its
# test games out of the real statistics. Both paths are printed at startup.
# To develop against a copy of real data, point DB_PATH at one.

# NOTE: NODE_ENV is NOT set here — this file is loaded by Vite, which sets
# NODE_ENV itself based on the build mode. For the Node server, NODE_ENV must
# be set in the shell. Use `npm run start:prod` which sets it automatically.

# ─── Frontend (Vite dev/preview server) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Host Vite's dev/preview server accepts requests for. Defaults to localhost
# for local dev. Set this to the deployed domain in production, e.g.:
# ALLOWED_HOST=tutto.example.com
ALLOWED_HOST=localhost

# Where `npm run dev` forwards /api and /socket.io. Defaults to
# http://localhost:3001, the local API server. Set this when something else is
# already answering on 3001 that a dev session must not touch — a real
# instance, say: the client-error reporter posts stack traces to /api, so a
# half-saved file on your machine would otherwise show up in its log. The
# socket proxy follows the same host (http→ws, https→wss).
# API_TARGET=http://localhost:4001
